Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.clips,{"olivia|Tom! Oh, thank goodness. Can you take her? Please? She hasn't slept since Sunday.":"","tom|...He's usually right about this stuff.":"","olivia|That. All night. And it's not just us. Lachlan’s toy truck is gone. Mr. Washington’s reading glasses. Marisol says every tennis ball on the block.":"","olivia|Bring her back tired! Please! Michael, can you grab Isla? She's licking the mailbox.":"","olivia|Bernadette from the Neighborhood Watch says it's squirrels. She has a clipboard about it. She's in Old Oak Park, at the south end of 2nd Ave.":"","tom|Tom. 3468. I've lived on 2nd Ave for six years.":"","penny|Bernadette. Neighborhood Watch Captain, nineteen years. And I'll say it, because nobody else will.":"","penny|Lookouts in the playground. A spy in the community garden. Somebody at the picnic tables stuffing their cheeks with anything that's not nailed down.":"","penny|Clear out those lookouts and your dog can dig. I'll be here. With my clipboard.":"","tnb|Babe, she has a corkboard with red string. I've never felt so seen.":"","tom|My shoes don't have laces.":"","skeeter|...You didn't see me. I'm a stick. Sticks don't talk.":"","tom|The garden is clear. Every tomato has exactly one bite out of it. That's a policy.":"","tom|Those are somebody’s sandwiches. Somebody’s whole birthday picnic.":"","tnb|Buddy. It's Los Angeles. It's seventy-four degrees.":"","tom|Eleven tennis balls. Those are Marisol’s.":"","tom|A pair of reading glasses. Those are Mr. Washington’s.":"","tom|A little yellow toy truck. Those are Lachlan’s.":"","tom|Mr. Washington reads the paper on his porch every morning. He's been reading the same headline for three days.":"","tnb|She hasn't eaten in three days, and she just ate your emergency bread.":"","tom|She'll only eat bread if I throw it. Still true. Still very picky. Still very athletic.":"","tnb|Babe. We're inside a tree. This is the second act of every horror movie I've ever seen.":"","tnb|That's what they always say in the second act.":"","tom|He's up there. And there's no ladder.":"","tnb|Everything connects to the jar, babe. That's how corkboards work.":"","tom|Very brave. Extremely brave. You'll be getting a lot of chicken.":"","tnb|It's a counterweight. Put enough weight in the bucket and the ladder comes down. Classic pulley.":"","bigone|That's what they WANT you to think.":"","tom|It's Los Angeles. Winter is a light jacket.":"","bigone|I'm the Chairman. Chairman Cheeks. Every acorn, every peanut, every shiny thing on 2nd Avenue comes up this tree. Because winter is coming.":"","tnb|It's a squirrel in a tiny tie, babe. I'm so scared and so delighted.":"","tom|You're going to be extremely sour about this.":"","tom|He's a starter. Sour is a compliment.":"","tom|Squirrels hoard shiny things. Squirrels don't tape things. Look at those corners.":"","tom|The sundial. The steamer. The sign-up sheet. Now my jar. Somebody keeps leaving these where we'll find them.":"","penny|Neighborhood Watch Captain’s report: case closed.":"","olivia|Tom! You found everything! Marisol’s balls, Mr. Washington’s glasses, Lachlan’s truck. He hasn't put it down. He's eating cereal with one hand.":"","penny|I'd like it noted that I was right.":"","tom|...That's not a pun. That's just a word.":"","tnb|It's a word with a pun in its heart.":"","penny|And these. Neighborhood Watch Vests. I give out one every nineteen years. Today I'm giving out three. Even the dog.":"","grace|Tata. TATA. Did you get my text? I sent it from Mom’s phone. She said I could. She said it after.":"","grace|Page says everything is fine. Page has said fine eleven times. I counted. Nobody says fine eleven times if it's fine.":"","page|...It's not fine. It started a week ago. It comes up from the Stacks, downstairs. The old part.":"","page|Then you're in charge of the signs. Here. The staff door is open.":"","page|Every book down there's whispering. Everything they ever heard. Seventy years of people reading quietly and thinking nobody was listening.":"","page|Please be careful. And please, don't answer the books. It only encourages them.":"","tom|I do talk to my bread. It's part of the process.":"","grace|Books can't look. They don't have... okay, that one has eyes.":"","grace|...That's actually true.":"","grace|I can read every sign. Rose can't read yet.":"","rose|Do the voice. Do Lamby’s voice.":"","tom|(a very small voice) Today I'm going to jump on everybody.":"","tom|Lamby’s Big Day. Page one. Lamby woke up and decided it was going to be a big day.":"","grace|Okay. That's actually a good book. Don't tell anyone I said that.":"","grace|That's all three cards, Tata. Card one, card two, card three. Three gold letters.":"","tom|...Let's focus on the encyclopedia.":"","grump|Actually, it's li-BRAR-y. Two Rs. Everybody says it wrong. Actually.":"","tom|The other one is why you're in charge of the signs down here.":"","grace|Tata. Am I a know-it-all? Be honest. Actually, don't be honest.":"","tom|It was terrified. Best scaring I've ever seen. Ten out of ten.":"","tom|You're the one whispering.":"","log|I'm the oldest book in the Stacks. Seventy years on this shelf. Nobody has checked me out. Nobody has opened me. Not once.":"","grace|Up, everybody. I'm in charge now.":"","tom|I'm adding it to the list.":"","log|...Fine. The end. I'll be quiet. I'm very good at quiet. I've had a lot of practice.":"","grace|It just wanted somebody to read it. That's all. All of it was because nobody read it.":"","page|Listen. It's quiet. Properly quiet. The good kind. The dictionaries are snoring.":"","rose|It's itchy. I love it.":"","page|Then we'll read it. Story time, Saturdays, out loud. And I think I know who should do the voices.":"","tom|\"I said yes for you. You're welcome. Bring the starter.\"":"","tom|A text from TNB. \"Babe. Bernadette signed you up for the 2nd Ave potluck. You're on bread. For forty people.\"":"","tom|I didn't fly here to serve forty people raw dough.":"","tnb|Hi. Missed you. Don't panic. Touch your stove.":"","tom|Bready Mercury’s dough has been rising since Thursday. Forty loaves. It needs a five hundred degree oven.":"","tom|...I haven't been home yet.":"","olivia|Bring her back fed! Please! Michael, Isla is eating the lasagna. It's a brick. She's eating a brick.":"","penny|The barn? It's been chained up for sixty years. Here. Committee key. I'm the committee. We're closing the boulevard for the tables. Bread by six.":"","tnb|Oh. Oh, babe. Look at it. The tracks are still in the floor. The time clock. The crew bench. I'm going to cry a little.":"","log|Why bother. It's just going to go out. Everything goes out eventually.":"","tnb|It dried out a little. Look. It's almost fluffy. It's a blanket again.":"","skeeter|Ironbelly asked for the flames, so I carried them. I'm a delivery draft.":"","tom|Who's Ironbelly.":"","tnb|That's three, babe. And that little steam motor by the turntable has three empty burners. Three. I can fix that.":"","skeeter|Wooooo. I said nothing. I'm just air.":"","tnb|That's either a boat or a stove. In a car barn, babe, it's a stove.":"","tnb|Babe. It's her. It's Nara as a lunchbox.":"","tom|It was on my plate. That's the rule. Food on her plate is suspicious. Food on my plate is a gift.":"","tom|And a picnic basket. Somebody packed it a very long time ago. It's somehow fine.":"","tnb|Babe. Somebody left lunch for the next guy. Sixty years ago. That's the nicest thing I've ever seen in a train yard.":"","tnb|Babe. It's warm in here. Like, really warm. Like, opening-the-oven-door warm.":"","bigone|...Who's in my Boiler Room. Nobody comes down here. Not since the last car went out. 1963.":"","bigone|Everybody up there has a little fire. I've been cold for sixty years. I only borrowed some.":"","bigone|I'm Old Ironbelly. 1912. Cast iron, all the way through. Biscuits for the night crew, every night, for fifty-one years. Cornbread on Fridays.":"","tom|Or. Forty loaves. Tonight. You're the only oven on 2nd Ave hot enough.":"","tom|Look at the corners. Not a speck of ash on it. Somebody put it there after the fire went out. I'm adding it to the list.":"","bigone|That's the crust. That's what crust does when it's done right. Here. Take my peel. Fifty-one years of biscuits. It wants to work again.":"","penny|Forty loaves. Six o’clock. On the dot. Potluck committee report: we're a success.":"","penny|The gumbo is hot. The casserole is hot. Everything is hot. I'd like it noted.":"","tom|...Thank you. I'll take very good care of it.":"","washington|He'd want it on somebody who went back in there and lit that stove. Here.":"","washington|Tom. Come here. This was my daddy’s. He drove the 7 line out of that barn for thirty years. Night run. He swore by the biscuits.":"","washington|I know you will. Now stand up straight. He'd say that too.":"","michael|Lachlan has eaten three rolls and fallen asleep in the bread basket. I'm leaving him there. He's happy.":"","tnb|The Moon Club. Babe. That's a secret society. I've seen this movie. Several times. It never goes well for the tall one.":"","tom|...There's no moon.":"","tom|There's no moon, and I have a gold letter. Okay.":"","grace|Also the moon is gone. Look. It's supposed to be a full moon. Luna said so. Luna is very upset.":"","rose|I'm six. Is six adults?":"","ellie|Girls. You're staying with me. I brought cards. I cheat. You'll learn a great deal.":"","boppy|I'm not wearing a tie.":"","deedee|You're wearing the tie.":"","boppy|...I'm wearing the tie.":"","deedee|Forty years I've lived in this town. Every full moon, the lights used to go on in that dome above Luna’s. Nobody I know has ever been invited. Not once.":"","ellie|The Moon Club. I haven't heard that name since 1971.":"","luna|...It wasn't a closet.":"","deedee|Oh. Oh, Tommy. It's beautiful.":"","boppy|Stairs. Of course it's stairs. Nobody take them fast.":"","deedee|It's FILTHY. Fifty years of dust. Somebody hand me a mop.":"","tom|The moon isn't gone. Something up in the Dome is pulling all of its light inside. Only a little gets out.":"","log|Ticket? Do you have a ticket? I'm holding this coat for ticket seven. She said she'd be right back.":"","deedee|Purple velvet. Tommy. That's Aunt Ellie’s coat.":"","deedee|We'll tell her, honey. She'll be so pleased. She'll pretend not to be. That's how you know.":"","boppy|Three mirrors. Three stands. One little moonbeam. I didn't drive a car for forty years without learning about mirrors.":"","boppy|Gin rummy with Deedee, fifty years. I've never won a hand. Not one. I know a sore loser when I see one.":"","boppy|Sunday. My house. Bring your own deck. You'll lose. I'll lose too. We can lose together.":"","tom|Then we'll ask. Nicely. After you give us the mirror.":"","mudling|Oh. Oh no. People. Don't look at me. I'm just here. With the wall. And this mirror. Which I'm hiding behind.":"","tom|(Tom doesn't take a picture. Tom takes four pictures.)":"","mudling|The Mirrorball. Up in the Dome. She hasn't stopped spinning in three nights.":"","deedee|Tommy. Over the bandstand. It's so BRIGHT. I can't look at it. I'm looking at it.":"","deedee|Honey, there's a whole town walking into hedges down there.":"","deedee|Oh, honey. Nobody has to turn off the lights. We'll come back. Every full moon. I'll bring crisp.":"","deedee|Somebody invited you up here, Tommy. Not her. She can't hold a pen. She's a ball.":"","deedee|Somebody who knew you'd come. And that you'd bring your mother.":"","tom|Somebody with a little clock. I'm adding it to the list.":"","rose|I won at cards. I cheated. Aunt Ellie said I'm a natural.":"","ellie|She is. It's frightening. Well? Was there a ball?":"","ellie|I left it at the last dance. I was in a hurry. I had a date with a man who turned out to be a disappointment. The coat wasn't.":"","boppy|I wore the tie. Everybody saw. Nobody can say I didn't wear the tie.":"","ellie|It hasn't fit me since 1972. Keep it, Tom. Somebody in this family should wear velvet properly.":"","rose|Can I come? I'll be good. I'll be medium good.":"","tom|There's no boarding group zero. I have flown Delta One forty times. I'd know.":"","deedee|Tommy, there was something else in the envelope. Stuck to the bottom. I didn't see it. I read it eleven times and I didn't see it.":"","amy|You're not taking my girls to a closed airport at midnight without me.":"","rose|I'm in group zero too. I decided.":"","amy|Fine. I have run through every airport in America. I've never missed a connection.":"","tom|A gate agent who makes the passengers fix the clock. I have flown Delta One forty times. That's a first.":"","log|Nobody has reached the front of me since 1989. I'm holding the hour hand. Nobody gets an hour without waiting for it.":"","amy|I don't wait in lines. I move to the front, and I say thank you to every single person on the way.":"","tom|I've been keeping a list. I have also been keeping the coins.":"","amy|Three hands. The clock still isn't moving. Tom. The slots round the face. There are seven of them.":"","tom|A well-traveled bag. We'll pick you up. After you give us the minute hand.":"","grump|The second hand is mine too. I'm not giving up a single second.":"","tom|Lounge etiquette. You get one armrest. The middle seat gets both. That's the rule.":"","bigone|If it's always midnight, the flight is never late. If the flight is never late, somebody might still come.":"","amy|My running watch hasn't moved in a day. I can't log a run. Do you understand what you've done.":"","bigone|Something for the gate clock. It's been in my bottom row since 1989.":"","bigone|...Fine. Flight Zero is cancelled. It was cancelled in 1989. I just didn't want to be the one to flip the flap.":"","bigone|For the smallest passenger in Group Zero. Junior pilot wings. I've been saving them for somebody.":"","grace|Tata. Tata. The jet bridge. There's a man.":"","rose|What's a layover?":"","grace|In a long coat. Like at the school. He's tipping his hat at you.":"","tom|It means this trip isn't over.":"","amy|Okay. It's twelve oh four. Mom has been holding Sunday dinner since midnight. Everybody to the cab.":"","boppy|Every clock in this house started at once. Eleven clocks. I didn't know we'd eleven clocks.":"","deedee|THERE they are. Tommy! The oven clock started blinking twelve oh one and I cried a little. Into the gravy. It's fine. It's seasoning.":"","tom|It's store-bought.":"","ellie|Sit. Tell me about the airport. Leave nothing out. I'll know.":"","justin|It's store-bought.":"","tom|I'll allow it. Tonight.":"","rose|Tata. Next time there's a layover, can I come?":"","rose|ICE CREAM! Come on, Tata! Let’s go!":"","deedee|Everybody sit. Everybody. Justin, you too. Ellie, that's Boppy’s chair. Boppy, that's my chair. Boppy.":"","tom|We get the scoops, we get the sundae, we're home by four.":"","tom|It's not a bigger puppy.":"","tom|The trees aren't talking. The freezer is. Eyes on the cones.":"","grace|Moo-rielle! You smell like mint. We'll talk about it later.":"","grace|Dice says nine. Nine scoops. Nine candles. Let’s go.":"","grace|Tata. She's SLIDING.":"","tom|We get the scoops, we get the sundae, we're home by four. Everybody ready?":"","tom|We're leaving. We're coming back. That's a promise, not a rule.":"","tom|She's frozen, not broken. Keep walking. Don't tip her.":"","grace|Up, up. It's my birthday. Nobody stays down.":"","boppy|I heard. I'm sitting. The knee.":"","boppy|They're in the oven mitt, Dee. You're wearing them. On your hand.":"","deedee|...So they are. Don't say anything.":"","boppy|I didn't. I said it to Tom.":"","deedee|Dairy free. Good. Now. Rose. Come here, sweetheart. Deedee's got you.":"","tom|Warm beats cold. Okay. What do we have that's warm.":"","deedee|Cold doesn't beat cold, Tommy. Warm beats cold. Always has. Ask any nurse.":"","boppy|The one that's looking at you.":"","boppy|Don't take the ghost one. The ghost one is MINE.":"","tom|Boppy's peppers. Red, redder, and one that's looking at me.":"","rose|Boo. I'm practicing.":"","boppy|(from the window) That's enough peppers! Leave the ghost one!":"","grace|Up. Gremlins. We're not losing to GREMLINS on my birthday.":"","tom|Rose, give me the... fine. Keep it. Don't lick it.":"","tom|Mr. Pistachio. He owns a creamery. He's basically a freezer scientist.":"","pistachio|You're back! Did you... oh. No scoops. And the little one looks defrosted.":"","pistachio|He kept everybody else's. He never got his own.":"","pistachio|I replaced him in the spring. Newer. Quieter. I unplugged him on a Tuesday and I didn't even say goodbye.":"","pistachio|Take these. Hot cocoa. My recipe. If you're going back up there, you'll want something warm in you.":"","pistachio|Here's the thing about a freezer, Tom. The outside is the soft part. The door. People stick things on it. Photos. Drawings. Report cards.":"","tom|Freezer. Sad. Never had a birthday. Stole everything. We're going back.":"","justin|The banner's done. Hold this. No, the other end. Don't touch the copper.":"","justin|It lights up. Every letter. I'm an electrician, Gracie. It was never going to just hang there.":"","amy|Okay. Listen to me. I've run thirty marathons and taught four hundred kids. You don't out-freeze a freezer.":"","amy|...We'll talk about the pepper later.":"","amy|And Moo-rielle. Go. Love you. Don't tip your sister.":"","amy|Pip, Moss and Dot are coming at four. Deedee's cake is done. All you need is nine scoops and one freezer.":"","grace|It's STILL my birthday. And you have my COW.":"","rose|I have a pepper in my pocket and I'm not afraid to use it.":"","tom|Nobody's afraid of the pepper, Rose. Everybody ready? Warm things out.":"","rose|He tried to freeze me AGAIN. I'm spicy now. He can't.":"","grace|Tata. He needs something on his door. Something that's HIS.":"","tom|Pair it to my phone. One tap. It's still on there.":"","grace|That's us. On your door. Happy birthday, Brain Freeze.":"","tom|Everybody ready? It's still her birthday.":"","grace|Then it's round two. Birthday Wish is ready. All three of us.":"","amy|TOM. Don't get in that cab.":"","bigone|...Fine. FINE. Take your little flames back. I'll be cold again. I'm used to it.":"","bigone|And look at me. I'm WARM again. I'm five hundred degrees. Do you know how long it's been since I was five hundred degrees?":"","bigone|And this jar. This jar smells like bread FOREVER. You feed it and it grows. It never runs out. It's the perfect hoard.":"","bigone|Fine. FINE. This meeting is adjourned. I'm going to go stare at a bird feeder.":"","boppy|I'm a sore WINNER. Who hasn't won yet.":"","boppy|Somebody up there is playing music. Very loud music. In 1971 they called that a nuisance.":"","brainfreeze|...It's warm. Why's the picture WARM.":"","brainfreeze|My lid. My LID. It's OPENING.":"","grace|TWO hearts this year! That's a record!":"","grace|Tata is in front. I'm in charge of choreography. It's my birthday. FIGHT!":"","grace|Tata! Sprinkle Street Creamery! The sundae! Mr. Pistachio said it'd be READY.":"","grace|Tata. On the dais. It's a book. A really, REALLY big book.":"","grace|That's SO annoying. Finish your SENTENCES.":"","grace|Tata. TATA. Deedee has a LETTER for you. It's GOLD. She won't let us open it.":"","grace|Up, up. It's a slug. We're not losing to a SLUG on my birthday.":"","grace|Up, up. It's still my birthday. We go AGAIN.":"","grace|Up. Everybody up. It's my birthday and NOBODY stays down on my birthday.":"","grace|WE are coming. All of us. I'm already packing. In my head.":"","grace|You can't just tell people’s secrets! That's the rudest thing a book can do! That's a RULE!":"","grump|Grrrumble. Something moved into my pond. It's COLD. I'm a POND grump, not an ICE grump.":"","log|...Next. NEXT! You. You're at the front. Somebody is finally at the front.":"","log|If nobody will read me, then I'll read THEM. Out loud. To everybody.":"","log|That was 1971. I haven't let go once. I'm VERY good at hanging on.":"","luna|And my telescope can't find the moon. It's not behind a cloud. It's not anywhere. It's just GONE.":"","grace|A book told everybody I sing in the shower. Which is PRIVATE. Also I'm very good.":"","grace|ADULTS ONLY? I'm basically an adult. I have a YouTube channel. I have a SKINCARE ROUTINE.":"","grace|Everything is from the olden days. That phone has a CORD. Rose. Rose, don't lick the phone.":"","grace|Forty people? Tata. That's a FEAST.":"","grace|I'm adding it to MY list. Mine has a chart AND a key now.":"","grace|I'm picking you up. Officially. You're claimed. I'm putting a sticker on you. It says GRACE.":"","grace|Mom, it's SO good. We have boarding passes. Well. Tata has one. And Sal has one. Group ZERO.":"","grace|No late fees. EVER? Tata. I'm going to take out every book. Every single one. Alphabetically.":"","grace|Not a little bit. ALL the books. At the same time. And they're saying THINGS.":"","grace|Okay. Everybody up. I'm in charge of getting up. Up, up, UP.":"","grace|Rose, she's a sign that talks. Like the one at the dentist. But MAD.":"","grace|She let us hold it. For one second. Then she took it back and said, careful, that's wax.":"","olivia|Tom. TOM. Nara is eating. Look at her. She's EATING.":"","olivia|Tom! Can you take Nara? She won't eat. Her dinner is cold, so she won't eat it. Michael warmed it in his hands. She still won't eat it.":"","page|Books overhear EVERYTHING. That's why we whisper in here. It was never for the people. It's for the books.":"","penny|And it all goes up THAT tree. The Old Oak. There's a little door in the trunk. I've heard a secret knock. Only bits of it.":"","penny|They said it's the weekend. I said it's the POTLUCK. They hung up. I've filed a report. With myself.":"","rose|...Hey. HEY. Nobody scares ME. I do the scaring. That's MY job.":"","rose|I'm a PILOT. I'm wearing them upside down. On purpose. It's a pilot thing.":"","rose|I'm at the front! I'm the FRONT! Do I win?":"","rose|Somebody took it out and didn't READ it? That's so sad.":"","rose|Tata. It's SNOWING. Inside.":"","tnb|Babe. Babe. They have a corkboard. With RED STRING. I've waited my whole life for this.":"","tnb|Because the bread. And we're TOASTING. It works on two levels.":"","tnb|I've wanted to go in there since I MOVED here.":"","tnb|Forty loaves, babe. FORTY. They're crackling. Listen to them. They're singing.":"","tnb|She wouldn't eat her own dinner. She ate YOUR dinner.":"","tnb|Right. Well, it's cold. Everybody’s is cold. I tried to light yours. The flame LEANED, babe. Sideways. Toward the boulevard. Like it wanted to leave.":"","tnb|Steam. We have STEAM, babe. I fixed a hundred-year-old turntable motor. I'm going to put this on my resume.":"","tnb|That's all three scraps. One acorn, two acorns, three acorns. It's a sequence, babe. It's ALWAYS a sequence.":"","toad|...Fine. FINE. Take it. I'll try a bite of something. Later. Maybe. If it's warm. And not touching.":"","toad|Deal me in. No. Wait. Don't deal me in. You're cheating. Everybody is cheating. The MIRROR is cheating.":"","toad|Ew. EW. Who are you. What's that. Is that a dog? Ew. Is that BREAD? Bread is the worst. Bread TOUCHES things.":"","tom|\"Babe. Potluck is TONIGHT. Forty people. You're on bread.\"":"","tom|\"It says THE MOON CLUB. Nobody gets invited to the Moon Club. I've lived here forty years. I love you to the moon and back. Call me.\"":"","tom|A text from Grace. \"TATA. The library is WHISPERING. Like actually. Page says it's fine. It's NOT fine. Come home.\"":"","tom|Seven slots. And I have seven gold coins. In a sock. In my bag.":"","tom|That's Bready Mercury. He's nine. You feed him flour and water, and then you SHARE the bread. That's the whole point of him.":"","tom|That's my house. That's my JAR. Why is my jar in the middle of everything?":"","tom|Those are pilot lights. The whole block’s pilot lights. Something down here is collecting them.":""});
Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.voices,{"amy":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"heavy Long Island accent","designed":false,"voice_id":"HLSHrV3D7Gp6sEFcHNev","name":"AoT Amy (Kind)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8}},"rose":{"voice_id":"ocZQ262SsZb9RIxcQBOj","name":"Lulu Lolipop - High-Pitched and Bubbly  (female, young, american, characters_animation)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"grace":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"","designed":false,"voice_id":"JVVJ6VsnUPJAdfGmEBGP","name":"AoT Grace (Gretchen)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85}},"deedee":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"","designed":false,"voice_id":"9UrcxKDUU0pvcnFhdfTU","name":"AoT Deedee (picked 2026-10-28)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85}},"boppy":{"voice_id":"QzTKubutNn9TjrB7Xb2Q","name":"Jerry B. - New York Italian Mobster  (male, middle_aged, new york, characters_animation)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":1},"direction":"deep gravelly voice","designed":false},"sal":{"voice_id":"gcJ5PkVgShIxtP5HgbZK","name":"AoT Sal","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his fifties with a thick Long Island New York accent, a slightly nasal, raspy, fast and friendly voice. Chatty taxi driver, warm and a little dramatic, proud of his one cab. Clean studio recording."},"log":{"voice_id":"DmA9AOv6Fsic2LQdqVVM","name":"AoT Log Lump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A sleepy cartoon log creature, very slow, deep, woody and drowsy voice, yawning between words, mumbly and content. Animated character voice."},"tom":{"voice_id":"cjVigY5qzO86Huf0OWal","name":"Eric - Smooth, Trustworthy","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"bigone":{"voice_id":"qDteMRfOWoUEc7kcfWvl","name":"AoT The Big One","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An enormous ancient cartoon pond fish, huge slow booming bass voice with gurgling bubbles, pompous and boastful but childlike and easily delighted underneath. Animated character voice."},"toad":{"voice_id":"jcb48kKcDpNXjAxnAP2c","name":"AoT Bog Toad","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A huge cartoon toad, deep croaky throaty voice with a rumbling ribbit, territorial and proud, a bit vain. Animated character voice."},"skeeter":{"voice_id":"3NkCp1SubvPIw3g0s7Rf","name":"AoT Skeeter Swarm","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A cartoon swarm of mosquitoes speaking as one, high-pitched, thin, whiny and buzzy voice with a nasal zzz on every s, nosy and impatient. Animated character voice."},"tnb":{"voice_id":"QPmHuIriDGOvu1d9U7wn","name":"SuperDale - a mid-age voice & Friendly  (male, middle_aged, us midwest, informative_educational)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"boomie":{"voice_id":"FgGtmhYdBou3a14mKYgx","name":"AoT Boomie","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her forties with a big, warm, rich singer’s voice, bubbly and motherly, slides into song mid-sentence, laughs from the belly. Clean studio recording."},"bean":{"voice_id":"zROpM0X5rfQMe4CN4C7f","name":"AoT Bean","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his late twenties with an upbeat, rambling, friendly American voice. A little scattered, quick bursts of words, cheerful and unbothered. Light and bright. Clean studio recording."},"carmen":{"voice_id":"8ncJvaxiyfELP457mBLS","name":"AoT Doña Carmen","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her sixties with a warm, firm, proud voice and a light Salvadoran Spanish accent. Runs a pupuseria, generous and no-nonsense, laughs easily. Clean studio recording."},"pistachio":{"voice_id":"LyoSZrqTSG25l7i0uBGl","name":"AoT Mr. Pistachio","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his late fifties with a warm, hearty Long Island New York accent, an ice cream shop owner who loves his regulars, booming friendly laugh, talks with his hands, a little dramatic about his scoops. Clean studio recording."},"mudling":{"voice_id":"E2hOWZ8x3nGJuQURP3SG","name":"AoT Mudling","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small, silly cartoon creature made of mud, gloopy gurgling voice with wet bubbly consonants, slow and sulky, childlike and a little sad. Animated character voice."},"brainfreeze":{"voice_id":"kYM9iwUI7t87mhAOBs1T","name":"AoT Brain Freeze","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A cartoon villain who is a walking chest freezer: a flat, cold, humming monotone with a slight metallic buzz, deadpan and sulky, slow and heavy, with a lonely sadness underneath that cracks through when he is surprised. Animated character voice."},"boomie2":{"voice_id":"rrjdoujYPDo3FGeRqm3Q","name":"AoT Boomie","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A young Black American woman in her late thirties to early fourties with a warm, rich, low alto voice, smooth and a little husky, deeper than most women’s voices. A gospel and soul singer, kind and bubbly, laughs from the belly, slides into song mid-sentence. Clean studio recording."},"grump":{"voice_id":"moX2FuSiiLmOw0uEq4OU","name":"AoT Pond Grump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A grumpy cartoon swamp creature, low gravelly grumbling voice, cranky and wet-sounding, easily offended, a big softie underneath. Animated character voice."},"dot":{"voice_id":"gYzudf4C0nXnEecqXK5t","name":"AoT Dot","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small woman in her forties with a quick, crisp, precise American voice, slightly nasal. Talks fast in short exact phrases like she is reading a tally sheet. Proud of her accuracy. Clean studio recording."},"la_woman":{"voice_id":"eLXwnyHT9UJHbuyheJ9m","name":"AoT LA neighbor (woman)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her early thirties with a relaxed, warm, slightly husky Los Angeles voice. Easygoing, wry, a little tired, friendly neighbor energy. Clean studio recording."},"michael":{"voice_id":"24fSFWvKYGI0zVR7L6JQ","name":"AoT Michael","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A tall man in his early forties with a calm, low, dry American voice. A tech dad holding two kids, patient, deadpan, quietly funny, a little tired. Clean studio recording."},"penny":{"voice_id":"C0jocNoR6bwrjLXwelto","name":"AoT Penny","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her forties with a fast-talking, bright, enthusiastic American saleswoman voice. Quick patter, playful, warm and a little pushy, every line a pitch. Clean studio recording."},"page":{"voice_id":"UnNThlnnIcLaHiWDpFdl","name":"AoT Page","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his forties, a librarian with a hushed, dry, whispery American voice. Speaks very quietly and precisely, mildly scandalized by everything, droll. Soft breathy whisper. Clean studio recording."},"olivia":{"voice_id":"3KdkB2LF6PUw0muuS0j7","name":"AoT Olivia","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her late thirties with a quick, bright, articulate American voice. A journalist and mom of two little kids, talks fast, wry and warm, always half distracted. Clean studio recording."},"luna":{"voice_id":"qCj5kMANfHcvCnzG1gVB","name":"AoT Luna","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her thirties with a dreamy, slow, wonder-filled American voice. Soft and spacey, drifting pauses, sincere awe with a touch of embarrassment. Clean studio recording."},"justin":{"voice_id":"Pp9gl3BrnVq62dIWU2sx","name":"AoT Justin (Long Island)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his early forties with an easygoing, friendly voice, Long Island born with a slight country twang. Goofy proud dad, handyman, sports fan, relaxed and warm, quick to laugh. Clean studio recording."},"gus":{"voice_id":"CcabrpeMRBXae9HlsCuq","name":"AoT Gus","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An old man in his seventies with a slow, warm, slightly creaky American voice. Deadpan and dignified, treats sitting on a bench like serious athletic training. Unhurried. Clean studio recording."},"oolong":{"voice_id":"2PhKaj7sDKqdDEhqQyhl","name":"AoT Oolong","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An elderly woman in her seventies with a warm, gossipy, conspiratorial voice and a light British accent. Leans in to share secrets, little cackle of a laugh, cozy and sly. Clean studio recording."},"washington":{"voice_id":"ARRjeRIXQjOrcraWRDoq","name":"AoT Mr. Washington","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An elderly man in his eighties with a deep, warm, slow voice and a gentle hint of Louisiana in it. A neighborhood storyteller on his porch, unhurried, kind, a little gravelly. Clean studio recording."},"ellie":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"","designed":true,"voice_id":"hZCpO8frcjUSQcVVhRiz","name":"AoT Aunt Ellie (Long Island, 2026-10-28)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85}}});
